  "description": "The $N: addressing case set, over one closed chain of three universes. Bare address = universe 1; $2:/$3: fetch the same coordinate in universes 2 and 3; $2:...1.1.3 fetches a scroll that exists only in universe 2; $3:...1.1.3 is a miss in a universe that lacks the scroll; $4: is a miss in a universe that does not exist. A miss returns the empty string from Chain::fetch, exactly like a present-but-empty scroll; the manifest's found flag (coordinate present in that member's phokenize list) is the only distinction.",
